# The daily backup of the local OmniRoute stack, started by omniroute-backup.timer.
#
# The work lives in ~/.local/bin/omniroute-backup: it copies the gateway's storage.sqlite through
# VACUUM INTO inside its container, packs that copy with the secrets and the manifest a restore
# needs, encrypts the tar with the age identity in ~/.ssh/omniroute-backup-key, rotates
# ~/.local/share/omniroute-backups and copies the archive to the personal OneDrive. A failed copy
# fails this unit. `omniroute-restore` brings an archive back; see .docs/omniroute-local.md.
#
# No [Install] on purpose: enabling this unit at boot would only add a second backup on machines
# that boot daily. The timer is what gets enabled -- it starts this unit.

[Unit]
Description=Encrypted backup of the local OmniRoute stack
Documentation=https://github.com/rios0rios0/dotfiles/blob/main/.docs/omniroute-local.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/omniroute-backup
